# 01 — Viewport 3D Module Architecture

## 1. Module Identity

```
Module ID:    viewport-3d
Slot:         viewport-main
Capability:   preview_3d
```

The `viewport-3d` module renders the physical domain, mesh topology, field quantities (scalar + vector), selection highlighting, geometry authoring overlays, and camera tools. It operates through a **domain-neutral render model** — it never sees `fdm` or `fem` strings.

## 2. Target File Tree

```
src/modules/viewport-3d/
  manifest.ts                       # Module manifest for kernel registry
  Viewport3DModule.tsx              # Module root: thin adapter, subscribes to store + hooks
  store.ts                          # Module-local Zustand: camera, dirty, display mode, grid layout
  components/
    ViewportSurface.tsx             # Canvas host + imperative renderer bridge
    ViewportToolbar.tsx             # Local display controls (wireframe, grid layout switch)
    ViewportOverlayStack.tsx        # Stacked overlays: legend, status chips, gizmo hints
    ViewportGrid.tsx                # Multi-pane layout (1×1, 1×2, 2×2, 1+2)
    ViewportPane.tsx                # Single pane: owns its SceneController instance
  hooks/
    useViewport3DResources.ts       # Aggregates topology/field/viz resource hooks
    useViewportCamera.ts            # Camera state, presets, serialization
    useDirtyRenderLoop.ts           # RAF scheduling gated by dirty reasons
    useViewportResize.ts            # ResizeObserver → dirty(resize)
    useViewportPicking.ts           # Mouse → raycasting → selection event
  renderers/
    SceneController.ts              # Three.js scene, camera, renderer, lights lifecycle
    MeshLayerRenderer.ts            # Topology geometry (surface mesh for FEM, cell cubes for FDM)
    FieldSurfaceRenderer.ts         # Scalar color mapping on topology
    VectorGlyphRenderer.ts          # Sampled arrow/cone instances
    SelectionLayerRenderer.ts       # Selection highlighting (outline, tint)
    WireframeLayerRenderer.ts       # Wireframe overlay
    AxesGridRenderer.ts             # Axes helper + ground grid
    AirboxRenderer.ts               # Airbox wireframe boundary
    ClipPlaneRenderer.ts            # Clipping plane visualisation
  resources/
    WebglResourceTracker.ts         # Registry: geometry, material, texture, buffer → dispose
    BufferPool.ts                   # Reusable typed array pool for field data
  model/
    viewport3DTypes.ts              # All TypeScript interfaces
    buildViewport3DRenderModel.ts   # Domain adapter output → Viewport3DRenderModel
```

## 3. Manifest

```typescript
import type { ModuleManifest } from "@/kernel/types";

export const viewport3dManifest: ModuleManifest = {
  id: "viewport-3d",
  title: "3D Viewport",
  version: "0.1.0",
  slots: ["viewport-main"],
  capabilityGate: ["preview_3d"],
  component: () => import("./Viewport3DModule"),
  contributes: {
    commands: [
      {
        id: "viewport-3d:toggle-wireframe",
        title: "Toggle Wireframe",
        scope: "viewport",
        defaultShortcut: "Z",
        run: /* toggled via store */
      },
      {
        id: "viewport-3d:reset-camera",
        title: "Reset Camera",
        scope: "viewport",
        defaultShortcut: "Home",
        run: /* camera reset */
      },
      {
        id: "viewport-3d:layout-single",
        title: "Single Viewport",
        scope: "viewport",
        run: /* layout change */
      },
      {
        id: "viewport-3d:layout-2x2",
        title: "Quad Viewport",
        scope: "viewport",
        run: /* layout change */
      },
      // ... more layout commands
    ],
  },
  emits: ["viewport:object-picked", "viewport:camera-changed"],
  listens: ["workspace:selection-changed", "session:field-revision-changed"],
};
```

## 4. Data Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  SessionStatus["useSessionStatus()"] --> Revisions["revision map"]
  Revisions --> MeshHook["useMeshTopology()"]
  Revisions --> FieldHook["useFieldData()"]
  Revisions --> VizHook["useVisualizationState()"]

  MeshHook --> DomainAdapter["createDomainAdapter()"]
  FieldHook --> DomainAdapter

  DomainAdapter --> RenderModelBuilder["buildViewport3DRenderModel()"]
  VizHook --> RenderModelBuilder

  RenderModelBuilder --> RenderModel["Viewport3DRenderModel"]
  RenderModel --> SceneController["SceneController"]
  SceneController --> Layers["Layer Renderers"]
  Layers --> Canvas["<canvas>"]
```

Key rule: **The renderer never receives API payloads.** Everything goes through domain adapters → render model builders → typed `Viewport3DRenderModel`.

## 5. State Ownership

| State | Owner | Update path |
|---|---|---|
| Camera (position, target, up, projection) | `viewport-3d/store.ts` | `useViewportCamera` hook, per-pane |
| Display mode (shaded/wireframe/...) | `viewport-3d/store.ts` | ViewportToolbar or command |
| Multi-pane layout config | `viewport-3d/store.ts` | ViewportToolbar or command |
| Selected quantity | Visualization resource (kernel-level) | Command registry |
| Topology revision | Session resource revisions | Realtime invalidation |
| Field revision | Session resource revisions | Realtime invalidation |
| Decoded field buffers | Resource cache + BufferPool | Resource hook |
| WebGL objects | `WebglResourceTracker` (imperative) | Renderer classes |
| Selected object | Kernel `SelectionController` | Explorer / viewport picking |
| Hover/probe position | Local ref (not state) | Pointer events |
| Dirty reasons | `viewport-3d/store.ts` (bitfield) | All above triggers |

**Forbidden patterns:**
- Decoded field arrays in React `useState` or Zustand.
- WebGL geometry/material/texture in any store.
- Importing inspector or explorer store from viewport module.

## 6. Module Root Component

```typescript
// Viewport3DModule.tsx — thin adapter
export default function Viewport3DModule({ kernel, moduleId, slotId }: ModuleProps) {
  const resources = useViewport3DResources(kernel);
  const renderModel = useMemo(
    () => buildViewport3DRenderModel(resources),
    [resources],
  );

  return (
    <section className="fm-viewport-3d" data-module-id={moduleId}>
      <ViewportToolbar />
      <ViewportGrid renderModel={renderModel} kernel={kernel} />
      <ViewportOverlayStack renderModel={renderModel} />
    </section>
  );
}
```

The root component:
1. Subscribes to resource hooks.
2. Builds a render model (pure transform).
3. Passes the render model to `ViewportGrid`.
4. Never touches Three.js or WebGL directly.

## 7. Lifecycle

### Mount
1. Module registered → capability gate passes → manifest lazy-loaded.
2. `Viewport3DModule` mounts, subscribes to resource hooks.
3. `ViewportGrid` mounts panes based on layout config.
4. Each `ViewportPane` creates a `SceneController` → Three.js renderer, scene, camera.
5. `SceneController` registers all WebGL resources with `WebglResourceTracker`.
6. `DirtyRenderLoop` starts but does **not** render (no dirty reasons yet).
7. First data arrives → dirty(topology + field) → first frame.

### Update (quantity switch)
1. Quantity command changes visualization resource.
2. Field hook detects revision change → fetches new field data.
3. `buildViewport3DRenderModel` produces updated `scalarField`.
4. `FieldSurfaceRenderer` updates buffer data (uniforms + attribute) — **no topology rebuild**.
5. dirty(field) → one frame rendered.

### Update (topology change)
1. Mesh rebuild triggers topology revision change.
2. Mesh hook fetches new topology binary.
3. `buildViewport3DRenderModel` produces updated `topology`.
4. `MeshLayerRenderer` disposes old geometry → creates new → registers with tracker.
5. `FieldSurfaceRenderer` also gets new geometry reference (field buffer may need re-upload).
6. dirty(topology) → one frame.

### Unmount
1. Module unmounts (e.g., user switches to 2D-only view).
2. Each `ViewportPane` calls `SceneController.dispose()`.
3. `SceneController` calls `WebglResourceTracker.releaseAll()`.
4. All geometries, materials, textures, render targets, buffers released.
5. Animation frame handles cancelled.
6. Resize observers disconnected.
7. Event subscriptions cleaned up by React hooks.

## 8. v1 Comparison

| Aspect | v1 (legacy) | v2 (this plan) |
|---|---|---|
| FDM/FEM handling | `discretization` prop fork in React tree | Adapter pattern: `FdmAdapter` / `FemAdapter` → uniform `RenderModel` |
| Layers | React wrapper components (`ArrowLayer`, `MeshLayer`) | Imperative renderer classes |
| Render loop | Always-on `requestAnimationFrame` | Dirty-driven: frame only on change |
| Resource tracking | None (manual dispose scattered) | `WebglResourceTracker` with counted registration |
| State | Giant `ControlRoomContext` + hooks + stores | Module-local store + kernel selection + resource hooks |
| Multi-view | Not supported | `ViewportGrid` with 1×1, 1×2, 2×2, 1+2 layouts |
| Picking | Mixed with rendering | Dedicated `useViewportPicking` with canonical selection events |
